      "message": "Checking for table values seems like something skrifa might get away with, but this seems the wrong level. Could we have the `colr` one be more like\n\n```\nfn has_any_colr_glyph(font_ref: \u0026BridgeFontRef, format: ColorGlyphFormat, glyph_id: u16) -\u003e bool {\n    font_ref\n        .with_font(|f| {\n            let colrv1_paintable \u003d f\n                .color_glyphs()\n                ...?; // ????\n        })\n        .unwrap_or_default()\n}\n```\n\nWith the ???? being there because `skrifa::color::ColorGlyphCollection` doesn\u0027t appear to have any way to state if it is empty? For the bitmaps it looks like `font_ref.xxxx().ok()?;` should work, since that\u0027s how we actually access them. In other words, the check should be as close as possible to when this will actually do to retrieve the values.",
