      "message": "\u003e  In other words, the check should be as close as possible to when this will actually do to retrieve the values.\n\nI assumed you mean \"_what_ this will actually do..\"? Updated to match and be closer to actual checks when retrieving the glyphs, instead of scanning for tags in the SNFT header.\n\nPlease see https://docs.rs/skrifa/latest/src/skrifa/color/mod.rs.html#398 - which shows that retrieving the `ColorGlyphCollection` does check for presence/readability of `colr()` first thing, so I think my updated approach gets fairly close to the read checks in Skrifa. Hope this works for you and we can avoid a round trip of adding a count function to `ColorGlyphCollection` and rolling Skrifa etc. \n\nAs an optimization, this is only intended as a cheap to determine necessary condition of color glyph presence, the sufficient condition is then checked separately.",
